From 7527ecab26c4839ebe60ecf8ebe43c2419aa23a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:44:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/27] browser: point the schema-first tier at an
 OpenAI-compatible engine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tier was Ollama-only, so the engine actually chosen for it could not be
called: there was no way to select another API. Engine is now explicit, with
Ollama as the default so no existing caller changes behaviour silently, and an
unknown engine name is refused rather than defaulted.

The egress route is unchanged: with_engine runs the same zone predicate in the
constructor, and the OpenAI-compatible call rides self.client, so adding an engine
does not add an egress path.

Credential handling: TALLOW_LLM_API_KEY, read at call time and never stored on the
extractor (so it cannot reach a Debug render, the disk schema cache, or a receipt),
never an argv value, never a .tl literal. A missing credential is refused as
EngineMisconfigured — new, and deliberately distinct from OllamaUnavailable,
because "not configured" and "not answering" need different fixes. Error text
quotes URL and status only, never a response body that could echo the request.

Which engine ran is recorded via run_evidence::record("llm_engine", ...), so it is
a fact about the run rather than an inference from configuration.

Verified: 5 offline tests — the chat-request shape, the response shape, rejection
of an Ollama-shaped response, the credential refusal, and the env-name contract;
browser::llm_extract's existing 35 tests still pass.
UNVERIFIED and stated as such: the live call — it needs a key, so the wire path is
plausible but not demonstrated.
